     1	# Relux Proxy
     2	
     3	Relux Proxy is a native macOS menu bar app for saved, independently controlled
     4	SSH dynamic SOCKS5 tunnels. Multiple profiles can run concurrently when they
     5	use different local ports. Every tunnel uses the system `/usr/bin/ssh`, so
     6	hosts, keys, jump hosts, and other options from `~/.ssh/config` continue to
     7	work; Relux Proxy does not parse or rewrite that file.
     8	
     9	The repository also contains the approved specifications and implementation
    10	backlog for a future macOS/iOS system VPN over SSH. That VPN is not implemented
    11	yet. Start with [the specification index](.spec/README.md),
    12	[the current-state inventory](docs/current-state.md), and
    13	[the saved task-board workflow](docs/project-management.md).
    14	
    15	## Use
    16	
    17	1. Open Relux Proxy from Applications. On the first launch after upgrading, the
    18	   previous `sshHost`, `sshAccount`, and `localPort` settings migrate into one
    19	   saved profile. A clean install starts with `administrator@relux` on
    20	   `127.0.0.1:1080`.
    21	2. Use **Add profile** to save another SSH-reachable IP address, hostname, or
    22	   `~/.ssh/config` alias and an explicit local SOCKS port. Ports must be unique
    23	   across saved profiles.
    24	3. Leave **Account** empty to let system OpenSSH use a matching config's `User`
    25	   or its normal login-user default. A non-empty account is passed as an
    26	   explicit `-l` override without changing the alias or SSH configuration.
    27	4. Choose **Connect** on each profile you want to run. Profiles with different
    28	   ports connect independently; a failure or occupied port affects only that
    29	   row.
    30	5. In Firefox, open **Settings → Network Settings**, select **Manual proxy
    31	   configuration**, and enter the endpoint shown on the chosen profile:
    32	
    33	   - SOCKS Host: `127.0.0.1`
    34	   - Port: the profile's saved port
    35	   - SOCKS v5
    36	   - Proxy DNS when using SOCKS v5
    37	
    38	6. Disconnect a profile before editing or removing it. Quitting Relux Proxy
    39	   stops every SSH process launched by the current app run. Profiles remain
    40	   saved, but tunnels do not reconnect automatically on the next launch.
    41	
    42	## Download
    43	
    44	The latest signed and notarized build always has the same asset name and URL
    45	(GitHub authentication is required while this repository is private):
    46	
    47	https://github.com/relux-works/relux-proxy/releases/latest/download/ReluxProxy.dmg
    48	
    49	Versioned DMGs and SHA-256 checksums are available on the GitHub Releases page.
    50	
    51	## Development
    52	
    53	Requirements: macOS 14 or newer and Xcode 16 or newer.
    54	
    55	```bash
    56	make lint
    57	make test
    58	make app
    59	make run
    60	```
    61	
    62	### Development tools
    63	
    64	| Command | Purpose | Output or effect |
    65	| --- | --- | --- |
    66	| `make lint` | Run strict `swift-format` checks over app and test sources. | Diagnostics only; source files are not modified. |
    67	| `make test` | Run the SwiftPM test suite. | SwiftPM build and test data in `.build/`. |
    68	| `make app` | Build and sign the macOS application. | `dist/ReluxProxy.app`. |
    69	| `make dmg` | Build the app, then package a disk image. | `dist/ReluxProxy-v<version>-universal.dmg`. |
    70	| `make run` | Build the app, then open it. | Opens `dist/ReluxProxy.app`. |
    71	
    72	The app is intentionally not sandboxed because it needs to launch the system
    73	SSH executable. Release bundles use the hardened runtime and are signed with
    74	the Relux Works Developer ID. The implemented legacy SOCKS behavior follows
    75	[the versioned multi-tunnel contract](.spec/legacy-socks-multi-tunnel.md).
    76	
    77	Contributors must follow [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md). Planned VPN work is
    78	tracked in `.task-board/`; no VPN implementation should begin without explicit
    79	approval of the generated plan.
    80	
    81	## Release
    82	
    83	Push a semantic version tag to build, sign, notarize, staple, attest, and publish both versioned and stable-name DMGs:
    84	
    85	```bash
    86	git tag -s v0.1.0 -m "Relux Proxy v0.1.0"
    87	git push origin v0.1.0
    88	```
    89	
    90	The release workflow expects `MACOS_CERT_P12`, `ASC_KEY_ID`, `ASC_ISSUER_ID`, and `ASC_KEY_P8` repository secrets. `ASC_KEY_P8` and `MACOS_CERT_P12` are base64 encoded.
     1	# Current state and future VPN boundary
     2	
     3	Last verified: 2026-07-28.
     4	
     5	## What exists
     6	
     7	The repository builds one SwiftPM macOS 14 executable, `ReluxProxy`, packaged by
     8	shell scripts as a menu bar `.app` and DMG.
     9	
    10	The app:
    11	
    12	- stores an ordered collection of profiles as one schema-versioned JSON Data
    13	  value under `legacySocksProfiles.v1`, with stable UUID identity and unique
    14	  explicit local ports;
    15	- migrates the legacy `sshHost`, `sshAccount`, and `localPort` values exactly
    16	  once, leaves those keys untouched for rollback, and never resurrects deleted
    17	  profiles after the migration marker is set;
    18	- owns one independent runtime session per profile, allowing multiple SSH
    19	  children and SOCKS tunnels to connect concurrently on different local ports;
    20	- launches `/usr/bin/ssh -N -C -D 127.0.0.1:<port>` with fail-fast, keepalive,
    21	  timeout, batch-mode, and quiet logging options;
    22	- passes an empty account as the bare host target, allowing system OpenSSH to
    23	  use a matching `User` setting (or its normal default); a non-empty account is
    24	  sent with `-l account` while the destination remains the bare host or alias,
    25	  which explicitly overrides only the SSH user;
    26	- accepts an IP address, hostname, or `Host` alias and lets the system client
    27	  apply matching `~/.ssh/config` behavior such as `HostName`, `Port`,
    28	  `IdentityFile`, and `ProxyJump`;
    29	- binds the SOCKS listener only to IPv4 loopback (`127.0.0.1`) and keeps a
    30	  separate trailing 4,000-character in-memory diagnostic for every session;
    31	- rejects duplicate saved ports and externally occupied loopback ports without
    32	  stopping or modifying another session or process;
    33	- reports connecting, connected, disconnecting, disconnected, and failed states
    34	  per row, with aggregate menu-bar status;
    35	- prevents profile edits and removal while that profile owns a starting,
    36	  connected, or stopping child;
    37	- stops every child it owns on normal quit and starts every saved profile
    38	  disconnected on the next launch, with no automatic retry or reconnect;
    39	- requires the user to configure a browser or other SOCKS-aware client manually;
    40	- intentionally runs outside the App Sandbox so it can spawn system SSH.
    41	
    42	Tests cover profile migration and persistence, command construction and account
    43	precedence, duplicate and OS port conflicts, concurrent independent lifecycle,
    44	stale callback protection, diagnostics, active mutation rejection, and
    45	coordinated shutdown. CI runs `swift test` and builds an ad-hoc-signed universal
    46	application bundle.
    47	
    48	Tagged releases import the Relux Works Developer ID certificate, build a
    49	universal app, sign the DMG, notarize and staple it, validate it with Gatekeeper,
    50	publish checksums/provenance, and upload both versioned and stable
    51	`ReluxProxy.dmg` assets.
    52	
    53	## What does not exist
    54	
    55	The current app is not a system VPN and does not contain:
    56	
    57	- iOS targets;
    58	- `NETunnelProviderManager` or packet-tunnel extensions;
    59	- a userspace TCP/IP stack or packetFlow bridge;
    60	- an embedded SSH implementation;
    61	- UDP or system DNS forwarding;
    62	- the remote `relux-relay` executable/protocol;
    63	- shared profile/Keychain state between host and extension;
    64	- Network Extension entitlements or provisioning;
    65	- TestFlight/App Store release automation.
    66	
    67	## Implemented legacy migration
    68	
    69	[the legacy SOCKS multi-tunnel contract](../.spec/legacy-socks-multi-tunnel.md)
    70	defines the implemented one-time migration, profile persistence, OpenSSH
    71	account precedence, port ownership, diagnostics, and independent lifecycle.
    72	Runtime state and reconnect intent are never persisted.
    73	
    74	The planned VPN product in `.spec/` remains a new architecture, not an
    75	incremental toggle inside the legacy SOCKS controller.
    76	
    77	For future VPN work:
    78	
    79	- the stable macOS release path must remain reproducible;
    80	- any migration from legacy SOCKS profiles to VPN profiles still needs its own
    81	  explicit product decision;
    82	- the system-SSH implementation may remain as a macOS legacy mode, be replaced,
    83	  or be retired only through a product decision;
    84	- SwiftPM tests and release history must not be silently discarded;
    85	- Network Extension code must not be backported into the current manual app
    86	  without the architecture and entitlement gates in `.spec/validation.md`.
